- Story & Context: The final track commemorates the legendary 1974 municipal shift change where the original time capsule was buried, using time-stretched ambient noise floor sampled directly from the degraded archival tape. A frantic, double-time neurofunk drum break tears through the middle of the piece like a runaway freight train, colliding head-on with a majestic, roaring tuba chorus that echoes down empty concrete corridors. As the sound decays into sea-like tape hiss, a lone voice sighs into a vintage ribbon mic: "Seventeen minutes past the shift, and nobody came to dig us out."
